Modularity (MOD):

MOD 01:
A] The robot should allow for additional modules to be easily removed (with basic hand tools) under 10 minutes from start to finish. Mechanisms concerning said removal should have very little compromises on strength, stability and reliability of use.

MOD 02:
A] The robot’s core should contain standardized mounting holes/ports for ease of design and universal mounting for modules.
B] The robot’s core should be designed with some future intent of sealant capabilities.

MOD 03:
A] The robot’s modules should be fairly universal in aesthetics and should try to retain similar dimensions for all terrains.

MOD 04:
A] The robot should provide standardized power connectors for all modules
B] The robot should be fit with a universal voltage rail for all modules (either 5V, 12V, 24V)
C] The robot should be fit with Safety measures for faulty modules e.g. fuses
D] The robot should be fit with a status board to monitor the status of all modules

MOD 05:
A] The robot should have software should provide diagnostic information on faulty modules
B] The robot should support 4 transport modules (terrain specific) and 4 additional modules

	

